WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.410
So, hello, I’m an aeronautical engineer.

2
00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:10.030
About my current position, I prefer to keep some professional details private.

3
00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.010
— All right, no problem.

4
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:18.970
So, in my opinion, the jury’s decision depends a lot on how you present your project

5
00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:21.530
and on your ability to defend it.

6
00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:27.290
Your answers to the questions, how relevant they are and how you phrase them

7
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.030
show how well you master the subject

8
00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.210
and your ability to justify your technical choices.

9
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.460
So, about a decision made too quickly:

10
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.020
I think you shouldn’t judge the deliberation only by how long it takes,

11
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.660
because the jury takes several things into account.

12
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:51.850
First, there’s the report, the work done, the presentation, and the answers to the questions.

13
00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:55.950
So my main advice is to be confident

14
00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.270
and convinced of what you have achieved.

15
00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:02.770
During the defence, your project is like a product

16
00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:06.690
that you have to sell to the jury at the highest possible price.

17
00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:11.710
So you need to know how to showcase your work, highlight its strengths

18
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:19.150
and defend your choices with confidence, while staying honest about the results you got.
